{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/observability.sh","reason":"Replace the cumulative count-offset delta with a timestamp cursor so each journal scan reads one interval instead of the whole retained journal; wall-clock bound the scans and publish nothing when a scan cannot complete. Also bound the IMDS curls, the git ls-remote mirror comparison and the data-disk debris du."},{"path":"infra/scripts/install-observability.sh","reason":"Render a finite TimeoutStartSec (strictly less than the 5-minute timer period) on the Type=oneshot service so a hung run cannot delete the timer's next elapse, plus Nice=10 and IOSchedulingClass=idle to match rebar-autodeploy.service."},{"path":"infra/systemd/rebar-autodeploy.service","reason":"Sibling of the same latch: Type=oneshot with no TimeoutStartSec driven by OnUnitActiveSec=2min. Add a finite start timeout."},{"path":"infra/terraform/user_data.sh","reason":"Cap journald SystemMaxUse so the worst-case corpus is bounded. Written and validated only, never applied; affects newly launched instances only."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_observability_journal_bounding_1205.py","reason":"New RED-first tests: journal read volume is invariant to retained-journal size, the delta stays correct under bounding, an unmeasurable scan publishes nothing and does not advance its cursor, and the rendered units carry a finite start timeout below their timer period."}]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1788564545035150049,"uuid":"d006bb93-9940-4982-87f0-4b48ff789906"}